're giving crappy jobs to get started  so you can work many many years and not  learn anything on the flip side your  best opportunity is to work with a  smaller company when you're working with  with an entrepreneur entrepreneurs  always have stuff that needs to get done  right we're never sitting there like I  have I have so much free time on my  hands I wonder what I could do right it  work we're crazy we're working like  crazy  always need help and so what I would try  to do is think about the type of  business that you want to start now I  have an entire zucca guide that walks  through this step-by-step and helps you  figure this out but this is kind of like  summarize it's called it's called work  to learn but that is the summarized  version go find the company that is  doing exactly what you want to do okay  and I look for company with ten  employees or less you want a small  company ten employees or less and go  work with them and get as close to the  entrepreneur founder as possible so when  you go you're going to get you're going  to get hired to do a certain set of  tasks right this is what you're going to  be hard to do XYZ but there's always  going to be opportunities it's always  going to be other things that need to be  done in that company and that's what you  want to sign up to do you want to get as  close to the founder as possible and  anytime something needs to get done at  that business you want to volunteer you  want to come with ideas and how you can  make the business stronger you want to  help out if it after hours free time  whatever it is just to get involved  because you're you're taking this job  not for the money but you're taking it  to learn so the more you can it get  involved with the entrepreneur who has  to deal with everything of running the  business then the faster your education  is going to be and maybe you're only  there six months maybe really there a  year before you learn what you need to  launch your business so it's much more  about the quality of the experience and  who you're working with in the size of  their business and the projects that  they give you the work on much more  important then how long we spend because  if you working at the wrong company  you're not going to be a good experience  good luck and believe those you watching  I love to hear if you've ever gone  through an internship program or if you  have a mentor who's helped you along the  way or what you've done to learn from  people who've gone through this ahead of  you leave it in the comments below so  you can help inspire other entrepreneurs  to we're facing the same problems you  guys like this video give it a thumbs up  below subscribe to the channel by  clicking on my face thank you guys so  much and I'll see you soon  you
 

